class A {
    static void show() {
        System.out.println("A");
    }
}

class B extends A {
    static void show() {
        System.out.println("B");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        A obj = new B();
        obj.show();
    }
}

=======================================sol==============================
show() is static.
Static methods are resolved using the reference type, not object type.
Reference type = A

Output: A
